Package: BayesPLCox
Title: Bayesian Inference for Cox Models via PL and GPL Likelihoods
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Tomohiro", "Ohigashi",
      email = "ohigashi@rs.tus.ac.jp",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Bayesian inference for Cox regression models based on
    Plackett-Luce (PL) and generalized/geometric Plackett-Luce (GPL)
    likelihood formulations. The acronym 'PL' reflects a dual interpretation:
    the classical Cox partial likelihood and the Plackett-Luce model for
    rank-ordered data, which are connected through a unified probabilistic
    framework. Posterior computation is performed using Gibbs sampling.
    The package supports fixed-effects and shared-frailty models, user-specified
    initial values, reproducible multiple-chain sampling, optional parallel
    chain execution, convergence diagnostics, and chain-specific trace plots.
